./LOGBOOK.md:155:### 2011 — libssh2 adapter bounds cancellation-ignoring injected work (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
./LOGBOOK.md:157:- REWORK: Timeout races now detach callers promptly while a bounded registry retains, cancels, and reports unfinished injected work until it actually returns. Upload keeps the libssh2 channel state machine actor-owned and applies one absolute deadline across open, source read, bounded drains, writes, EOF, and exit; only the injected source read is detached. External signer work follows the same visible ownership rule instead of making teardown wait indefinitely.
