./LOGBOOK.md:161:### 1943 — libssh2 adapter closes review round 5 fatal teardown and ownership gaps (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
./LOGBOOK.md:162:- ROOT CAUSE: Fatal socket failures were mapped inconsistently and could leave an apparently usable transport; automatic keepalive used its reply deadline while waiting behind KEX; teardown queues and task snapshots could grow or report optimistic zeros; and one-shot channel cleanup could discard a live libssh2 pointer after `EAGAIN`.
./LOGBOOK.md:163:- REWORK: One privacy-safe failure path now tears down every lane-fatal socket error. Automatic keepalive defers behind an active rekey and starts a fresh reply deadline after gate admission. Session/channel admission is capped, shared drains and teardown use single-flight tasks, and teardown cancels and joins all owned work before clearing handles. Channel close/free remains tracked until libssh2 confirms disposal; cleanup failure retains ownership for session teardown.
./LOGBOOK.md:164:- NONBLOCKING CLEANUP: A terminal socket enters an abort-drain mode that feeds EOF to receives and consumes only libssh2's already-retained outbound bytes. This lets the engine complete its nonblocking destructors without network I/O or fabricated operation success. Session destruction is bounded; failure remains explicit and keeps ownership visible rather than claiming a closed baseline.
./LOGBOOK.md:166:- VERIFICATION: `swift test --filter LibSSH2` passes 35 tests/3 suites; `make validate-core` passes 369 tests/31 suites plus build and boundary checks; `make validate-libssh2`, source tamper gates, and the dual-architecture extension-safe macOS provider/harness matrix exit 0. Strict recursive Swift format and diff checks pass. Logs use task-scoped `*-06.log` or later names under `.temp/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/`.
./LOGBOOK.md:168:### 1858 — libssh2 adapter closes review round 4 cancellation and cleanup gaps (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
./LOGBOOK.md:172:- VERIFICATION: `swift test --filter LibSSH2` passes 27 tests/3 suites; `make validate-core` passes 361 tests/31 suites plus build and boundary checks; strict Swift format and diff checks pass; `make validate-libssh2`, source tamper gates, and the dual-architecture extension-safe macOS provider/harness matrix all exit 0. Logs use the task-scoped `*-05.log` names under `.temp/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/`.
./LOGBOOK.md:174:### 1824 — libssh2 adapter preserves operation scope and nonblocking argument identity (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
./LOGBOOK.md:175:- ROOT CAUSE: Channel read/write timeout cancellation shut down the shared socket bridge; channel opens rejected `rekeying` before entering the session gate and started their deadline only after gate admission; each rekey caller owned the connection-global KEX; and concurrent writes could resume libssh2's single per-channel write state with a different payload after `EAGAIN`. Credential results were checked against factory capabilities but not the caller-provided allowlist.
./LOGBOOK.md:178:- VERIFICATION: `swift test --filter LibSSH2` passes 23 tests/3 suites; strict Swift format and `git diff --check` pass; `make validate-core` passes 357 tests/31 suites plus build and boundary checks; `make validate-libssh2`, `make test-libssh2-source-gates`, and `make native-apple-matrix` all exit 0. The four M3 semantics remain explicit `unsupported` states owned by `TASK-260728-3cveay`.
./LOGBOOK.md:180:### 1758 — libssh2 adapter loopback conformance closes review round 2 (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
./LOGBOOK.md:181:- ROOT CAUSE: libssh2 keeps channel-open and reply-requiring global-request nonblocking state on the shared session, so actor reentrancy across `EAGAIN` allowed a second open to resume the first open's state. The custom send/receive callback ABI also requires negative socket errors directly; returning `-1` plus `errno=EAGAIN` made ordinary backpressure appear as a disconnect.
./LOGBOOK.md:184:- VERIFICATION: Strict recursive `swift-format` and `git diff --check`, `make validate-core` (353 tests/31 suites), `make validate-libssh2`, `make test-libssh2-source-gates`, and `make native-apple-matrix` all exit 0. `task-board validate` exits 0 and reports only the known story aggregate mismatch while this child is in development; no status or unsupported semantic is bypassed.
./LOGBOOK.md:186:### 1454 — libssh2 adapter review rework closes async ownership gaps (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
./LOGBOOK.md:187:- ROOT CAUSE: Actor isolation serialized synchronous libssh2 calls but not the socket service work awaited between `LIBSSH2_ERROR_EAGAIN` retries. Reentrant progress calls could snapshot the same outbound prefix, issue duplicate writes, and later remove inconsistent byte counts; suspended operations also retained channel/session pointers while teardown could free them.
./LOGBOOK.md:190:- VERIFICATION: Focused adapter coverage grew from 7 to 11 tests, adding forced overlapping socket writes (exact bytes, maximum concurrency one), joined signer cancellation, resolution timeout phase/counter evidence, and 20 repeated connect-cancel resource baselines. Strict format/diff checks, `make validate-core` (349 tests/30 suites), `make validate-libssh2`, source tamper gates, and the dual-architecture extension-safe Apple matrix all exit 0.
./LOGBOOK.md:193:### 0351 — Pinned libssh2 adapter joins the macOS provider and harness graphs (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
./LOGBOOK.md:194:- IMPLEMENTATION: `ReluxTunnelLibSSH2Adapter` is the sole Swift target importing the pinned static libssh2/OpenSSL XCFramework. A serialized transport actor drives custom send/receive callbacks in nonblocking mode over the injected `SSHTCPConnection`; bounded async bridges turn socket and external-Keychain-signer progress into `LIBSSH2_ERROR_EAGAIN` without blocking a provider executor.
./LOGBOOK.md:196:- DECISION: Consumer-driven receive credit, RFC channel-open reasons, exact exec-exit presence/`coreDumped`, and deep server-KEX/keepalive reporting are all emitted as `unsupported`, owned by `TASK-260728-3cveay`. Client rekey, server-rekey protocol handling, bounded channel I/O, exec/stdin upload, and forced `keepalive@openssh.com` transmission remain implemented M0 behavior; no unavailable value is inferred from libssh2 internals.
./LOGBOOK.md:197:- ANOMALY: Xcode's generated package scheme copied both library-style XCFramework module maps to one custom `Release/include/module.modulemap`, producing a deterministic multiple-producer error once the libssh2 and native-fixture graphs met. The Apple matrix now keeps Xcode's existing device/simulator/native checks and uses isolated dual-architecture SwiftPM builds with `-application-extension` for the macOS provider/harness; the stripped release harness check verifies libssh2's intentionally hidden local rekey symbol separately from exported HEV symbols.
