./LOGBOOK.md:953:### 1208 — libssh2 adapter hits third-round channel/exec/window API boundary (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
./LOGBOOK.md:957:- ROUTING: This is the third fork-gap round anticipated by TASK-260720-2sltje. Do not add a partial/mock-only adapter. Recommend failing libssh2 red at M0 unless its value justifies one explicitly approved consolidated fork extension for manual windows, typed open failures, and lossless exec-exit metadata; the alternative is an explicit M0-to-M3/common-contract revision. Exact evidence and resume decision are attached as `TASK-260715-1ozsb6_third-public-api-blocker.md`.
./LOGBOOK.md:959:### 1200 — Bounded libssh2 observation fork clears the remaining public-API clauses (TASK-260720-2sltje)
./LOGBOOK.md:960:- DECISION: The existing libssh2 patch remains a single allowlisted six-file delta. It adds typed server-initiated KEX `STARTED`/`SUCCEEDED`/`FAILED` observation with a monotonic generation and one bounded, nonblocking reply-correlated global-request operation; packet ordering, encryption, MAC, KEX algorithms, and crypto implementations remain unchanged.
./LOGBOOK.md:963:- ANOMALY: The broader pre-existing HEV Apple matrix stops before any Xcode build because `HevSocks5Tunnel.xcframework` contains macOS 10.14 and 11.0 object minima while its manifest requires only 10.14. This artifact is outside the libssh2 delta; the task-specific XCFramework inspection and required `make validate-core` gates pass.
./LOGBOOK.md:965:### 1145 — libssh2 adapter remains blocked on server-rekey observability and keepalive replies (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
./LOGBOOK.md:966:- BLOCKER: The accepted `libssh2_session_rekey` fork clears client byte/time/manual trigger initiation only. The exact public header exports no KEX lifecycle callback or generation query. Pinned libssh2 handles inbound `SSH_MSG_KEXINIT` entirely inside private `packet.c`/`transport.c` state, so the adapter cannot truthfully emit `.serverInitiated`, mark `activeKeyExchange`, increment generation, or distinguish server-KEX success/failure through the public boundary.
./LOGBOOK.md:967:- BLOCKER: `libssh2_keepalive_send` writes `keepalive@libssh2.org` with `want_reply=1` but returns after queueing and stores no outstanding request or reply outcome. The public API exposes no generic reply-requiring global request or request-success/failure correlation. Consequently the adapter cannot measure reply RTT, enforce reply timeout/miss allowance, or distinguish acknowledgement from silence.
./LOGBOOK.md:968:- EVIDENCE: The public macOS XCFramework exports only `libssh2_session_rekey`, `libssh2_keepalive_config`, and `libssh2_keepalive_send` among relevant symbols. `keepalive.c:52-96` contains no reply wait/state; inbound server rekey is private at `packet.c:1336-1369` and `transport.c:407-425,1039-1048`. Trace callbacks are unavailable in non-debug builds and are not a supported protocol API.
./LOGBOOK.md:969:- ROUTING: Do not report these gates green or build a mock-only partial adapter. Recommend a separately reviewed minimal fork extension exposing typed server-KEX lifecycle plus a nonblocking reply-correlated global-request/keepalive API; alternatives are explicitly failing the libssh2 candidate or revising the mandatory contract. Exact options and resume decision are attached as `TASK-260715-1ozsb6_server-rekey-keepalive-blocker.md`.
./LOGBOOK.md:971:### 1115 — Minimal libssh2 public client-rekey fork clears the adapter blocker (TASK-260720-3vwls7)
./LOGBOOK.md:972:- DECISION: Pinned libssh2 `a34302491c164d53c900fec9b3cbb050ecebe719` carries one allowlisted two-file patch: `include/libssh2.h` publicly declares `libssh2_session_rekey`, and `src/session.c` adds a null-checked, nonblocking-friendly `BLOCK_ADJUST` wrapper over the existing `ssh2_kex_exchange(session, 1, &session->startup_key_state)`. No crypto, algorithm, packet, channel, or private-header surface changed.
./LOGBOOK.md:973:- SUPPLY CHAIN: The builder verifies libssh2 and OpenSSL 3.5.7 archive SHA-256 values before extraction or patch application, checks source-license hashes, rebuilds five static Apple architecture slices, emits the combined BSD-3-Clause/Apache-2.0/acknowledgement notice, and fails closed on patch/hash/path drift. Two clean rebuilds produced byte-identical XCFramework artifact locks.
./LOGBOOK.md:974:- VERIFICATION: The public-header-only C integration test drove the wrapper through three `EAGAIN` results, observed client-initiated NEWKEYS installation, then forced OpenSSH `RekeyLimit` server-initiated NEWKEYS and proved post-rekey channels remained usable. Fork verify/rekey/source-tamper gates, Swift public-module packaging test, native seam tests, strict Swift format, 62 core tests, and `swift build` pass; `ReluxTunnelCore` remains free of libssh2/OpenSSL imports.
./LOGBOOK.md:976:### 1030 — libssh2 adapter stops on absent public client-rekey API (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
./LOGBOOK.md:977:- BLOCKER: Exact pinned archive `a34302491c164d53c900fec9b3cbb050ecebe719` reproduced SHA-256 `744ba3e9…c87c`. Public `include/libssh2.h` has no rekey operation; initial `libssh2_session_handshake` calls private `ssh2_kex_exchange(..., reexchange=0)`, while only inbound `SSH_MSG_KEXINIT` reaches private `ssh2_kex_exchange(..., reexchange=1)` from `src/packet.c`.
./LOGBOOK.md:979:- ROUTING: Recommend recording libssh2 red/failed at this pin. The alternative is a separately authorized, audited libssh2 fork/public rekey hook (or a future upstream pin followed by full re-audit). Exact evidence and tradeoffs are attached as `TASK-260715-1ozsb6_libssh2-rekey-blocker.md`.
./LOGBOOK.md:1034:- MILESTONE: Audit accepted → `done`. Every load-bearing claim reproduced from upstream: tag→commit pins for both candidates plus all six transitive deps (ls-remote), all three archive SHA-256 and both license hashes (fresh downloads), 16 MiB window `SSHChannelMultiplexer.swift:211`, internal `_rekey()` `NIOSSHHandler.swift:511`, libssh2 window APIs and direct-tcpip hardcode `src/channel.c:384,457`, unexported reexchange `src/packet.c:1369`, version-macro anomaly, six CVE fix commits confirmed ancestors of `a343024`, GHSA advisories via API, exactly 679 libssh2 commits/12mo.
./LOGBOOK.md:1039:- SECURITY: SwiftNIO SSH is pinned to `0.14.1` / `31cdc3c`, which fixes critical CVE-2026-43798, with resolved Swift Crypto `4.5.1` and SwiftNIO `2.101.3` security-patched transitives. libssh2 release `1.11.1` is not a clean baseline because six advisories were fixed after release; the candidate is pinned to untagged `1.11.2_DEV` commit `a343024` containing all six fixes, with OpenSSL `3.5.7`. Re-audit on a signed libssh2 1.11.2+ release is mandatory.
./LOGBOOK.md:1040:- FINDING: SwiftNIO SSH hardcodes each child receive-window target to 16 MiB and exposes client `_rekey()` only internally. libssh2 exposes generic per-channel initial/remaining/adjust APIs, but its direct-tcpip helper fixes the 2 MiB default and it likewise has no public client-rekey API or automatic byte/time threshold.
./LOGBOOK.md:1042:- RISK: libssh2 master issue #2023 contains an unresolved AEAD correctness report whose specific leak interpretation is disputed. Treat it as an ASan/packet-content experiment, not a proven leak or a reason to prejudge the engine.
