+### 2225 — Keepalive aggregate coverage synchronizes on emitted events (BUG-260811-3qdo3e)
+- ROOT CAUSE: A fresh post-review aggregate gate reproduced one final in-scope test race at the historical run-13 position. `automaticKeepaliveSurvivesLongRekey` used at most 500 scheduler yields before reading each `keepalivesSent` counter. Under aggregate load, the automatic task had not emitted `.keepaliveSent` before either assertion, even though the fatal keepalive self-join was fixed and the suite exited normally. Fixed yield counts are not a synchronization boundary.
+- IMPLEMENTATION: `SuspendingRekeyObserver` now counts production `.keepaliveSent` events and resumes continuation-backed threshold waiters. The positive long-rekey test awaits the first and second emitted events before asserting the corresponding transport counters. Manual-clock advancement, rekey suspension, scoped cancellation, no implicit idle timeout, fatal teardown ownership, and the TASK-260715-1u2vpc algorithm matrix are unchanged; no sleep, timeout, skip, or wall-clock mask was added.
+- VERIFICATION: The four lifecycle regressions pass together 30/30 consecutive focused runs. A final reset-on-any-failure streak passes 20/20 unfiltered `swift test --skip-build` runs with 427 tests in 35 suites per run and 16–18 second durations, including historical runs 13, 16, and 17. `make validate-core`, `make validate-libssh2`, warning-free recursive Swift format lint, and `git diff --check` exit 0. The sshd listener set before and after remains the same older PIDs 1330 and 34815.
+- ANOMALY: The first fresh streak reset at run 7 with an unrelated HEV association snapshot assertion; the exact HEV case immediately passed focused. The next streak reset at run 13 with the reproduced keepalive counter race above. Both failing exit-1 logs are retained and neither run was counted toward the final streak.
+
 ### 2203 — Reviewer aggregate gate exposes a separate LibSSH pressure race (BUG-260811-3qdo3e)
 - REVIEW: The scoped cancellation test plus the positive and fatal automatic-keepalive regressions pass together with exit 0, and inspection accepts the no-self-join ownership fix, zero-resource assertions, and retained TASK-260715-1u2vpc algorithm matrix.
 - GATE: A reviewer-owned unfiltered streak passed 16 consecutive 427-test runs, including historical hang positions 13 and 16, then run 17 exited 1 because `channelOperationPressureIsBounded` observed `.cancelled` instead of `.resourceLimitExceeded`. The unchanged pressure test reproduced independently after nine focused passes; focused run 10 exited 1 with the same mismatch. The mandatory 20-run aggregate gate therefore remains failing even though the cancellation and keepalive cases passed in the failed aggregate run.
